---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import VenueCard from '../../components/VenueCard.astro';
import NewsletterBlock from '../../components/NewsletterBlock.astro';
import { routeSlug } from '../../lib/editorial';
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, absUrl } from '../../lib/schema';

const allVenues = await getCollection('venues');

// Cottages - self-contained, mostly hinterland, dog-friendly winter-fireplace format
const cottageSlugs = [
  'blue-moon-cottages',
  'mp-beach-club-cottages',
  'hideaways-red-hill',
  'birch-creek',
  'brewers-cottage',
];

// B&Bs - host-led, breakfast-included, named-host format
const bnbSlugs = [
  'villa-mallorca',
  'plantation-house-whitecliffs',
  'the-orchard-red-hill',
  'driftaway-on-dundas',
  'arthurs-views',
  'mantons-creek-estate',
  'treetops-red-hill',
];

const allSlugs = [...cottageSlugs, ...bnbSlugs];
const venues = allSlugs
  .map((slug) => allVenues.find((venue) => routeSlug(venue) === slug))
  .filter((venue): venue is NonNullable<typeof venue> => Boolean(venue));

const cottageVenues = cottageSlugs
  .map((slug) => allVenues.find((venue) => routeSlug(venue) === slug))
  .filter((venue): venue is NonNullable<typeof venue> => Boolean(venue));

const bnbVenues = bnbSlugs
  .map((slug) => allVenues.find((venue) => routeSlug(venue) === slug))
  .filter((venue): venue is NonNullable<typeof venue> => Boolean(venue));

const breadcrumbItems = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Stay', href: '/stay/' },
  { label: 'B&Bs & Cottages' },
];
const breadcrumbSchema = buildBreadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: absUrl('/') },
  { name: 'Stay', url: absUrl('/stay/') },
  { name: 'B&Bs & Cottages', url: absUrl('/stay/cottages/') },
]);
export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="B&Bs and Cottages Mornington Peninsula · Peninsula Insider"
  description="The best cottages and B&Bs on the Mornington Peninsula - self-contained hinterland cottages with fireplaces, and named-host B&Bs where the host is the reason to go."
  section="stay"
  canonical="https://peninsulainsider.com.au/stay/cottages/"
  modifiedTime="2026-05-08"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />
  <article class="article">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="article__title">B&Bs and Cottages on the Mornington Peninsula</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The two formats answer different briefs. A cottage is self-contained: you arrive with groceries, the dog, and no obligations - a wood fire, a kitchen, a fenced garden, and the door closing behind you. A B&B runs on a different logic, built around a host, a breakfast, and a small house where someone has thought about the day ahead of you. Both formats outperform the hotel in shoulder season. Both are mostly hinterland, not coast.</p>
        <p>The winter wood-fire weekend is the strongest use case for cottages. Properties across Main Ridge, Red Hill, and Rye with confirmed fireplaces draw the highest proportion of repeat visitors in the category. Load up at the Red Hill Community Market on Saturday morning, light the fire by afternoon. The dog weekend is the second clear use case: Blue Moon, MP Beach Club, and Birch Creek are the most explicitly dog-welcoming.</p>
        <p>The named-host B&B pattern: at a cottage, the owner is largely invisible after key handover. At a B&B, the host is the reason the format works. Paul and Sheree at Villa Mallorca, Charles at Plantation House, Helen and Frank at The Orchard - the host is not incidental to the stay, it is the product.</p>
        <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--soft)">Last fact-verified: 7 May 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="venues" id="cottages">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="venues__header">
        <div>
          <p class="label label--accent">Cottages</p>
          <h2 class="venues__title">Self-contained Peninsula cottages</h2>
          <p class="venues__sub">Fireplaces, kitchens, dog-friendly yards - strongest in autumn and winter when the hinterland earns its keep.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/journal/dog-friendly-accommodation-mornington-peninsula/" class="venues__link">Dog-friendly stays →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="venues__grid">{cottageVenues.map((venue) => <VenueCard venue={venue} hrefPrefix="/stay" />)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="venues" id="bnbs">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="venues__header">
        <div>
          <p class="label label--accent">B&Bs</p>
          <h2 class="venues__title">Named-host Peninsula B&Bs</h2>
          <p class="venues__sub">Breakfast included, host-led, four rooms or fewer - at their best midweek when you get the full attention of someone who has thought about your morning.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/stay/winery-accommodation/" class="venues__link">Wine-country stays →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="venues__grid">{bnbVenues.map((venue) => <VenueCard venue={venue} hrefPrefix="/stay" />)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NewsletterBlock />
</BaseLayout>
